Ah, the fickleness of nethack. . .

Ocean, a daring young woman on her first assignment as a Valkyrie was sent
plumbing the depths of the Great Donjon of NetHack after the Amulet of
Yendor.
After staggering around the first level for a while--hot, discouraged, and
thirsty--she came upon what must surely be a boon from Loki.  There in
front of her was a sparkling clean fountain of cool water.  She bent over
to take a sip, when, with a sound of a many-throated yell, a huge demonic
form appeared in front of her!!!
Terrified at being confronted with a being of such monstrous power, she
began to panic, until the booming roll of it's voice informed her of its
pleasure with her. She had been granted at wish!!
She had heard that mail made from the scales of a dragon, particularly a
gray one, was excellent defense, important for one of such modest puissance
as herself.  "So mote it be!" boomed the demon, and she found herself in
possession of the finest set of armor she had ever seen.

Before long, she had found the entrance to the next level, whereupon she
immediately found another fountain, thinking craftily (Loki would have been
proud..) she decided to test Fate once again.  She sipped of the cool
waters.  Again, she was entreated to the rumbling roar of a demon's
presence.  Trembling in fear and hopefulness, her daring was not in vain.
Once again, a demon was pleased to be released after so long an
imprisonment. She became more daring in her wishing, desiring that most
potent of blades, the evil Stormbringer.  In a trice, the demon had
disappeared, and blink'd back into existence bearing the moaning runesword
in it's gnarled fist. "Beware," it said, "For much power in the hands of
one so young must needs to to one's heart, rather than one's head."

Ocean would not hear. Giddy with the strength her new acquisitions gave
her, she proceeded on a orgy of slaughter, penetrating deep into the
dungeon.

Alas for Ocean, her inexperience betrayed her as she wandered down a
corridor and bumped into what looked like a giant upended cubical mold of
gelatin.  All it seemed to be able to do was wiggle menacingly at her.
"Easy meat!" she thought as she sank her blade deep into it's wobbling
form...

Thirgon, Green-Elf courier to the High King, was conveying a message to the
King's Consort on this particular level of the dungeon, when he came upon a
sad sight indeed. A young maiden frozen in her tracks by that most
insidious of creatures, the gelatinous cube.  He sighed as he wandered over
to dispatch the beast and free the maiden. But lo! He noticed the faintly
whining runesword and the markings of Loki upon this, not-so-fair maiden.
"Ach! More chaos! More evil!"  Morose at the waste of such a tender young
life, he proceeded to unsheathe his tempered blade and plunge it through
the side of the hapless valkyrie.  "Alas, that you must die, fair maiden."

Thirgon wandered off humming a quiet tune about the joys of miruvior,
paying no heed to the crumpled form behind him. If he hurried, he would
reach the Elvenhalls in time for the second round of song...


